, "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Gorillaz", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "britpop": {"genre": "britpop", "country_code": "mx", "country_name": "Mexico", "summary": "Britpop is a subgenre of alternative rock that originated in the United Kingdom. Britpop emerged from the British independent music scene of the early 1990s and was characterised by bands influenced by British guitar pop music of the 1960s and 1970s. The movement developed as a reaction against various musical and cultural trends in the late 1980s and early 1990s, particularly the grunge phenomenon from the United States. In the wake of the musical invasion into the United Kingdom of American grunge bands such as Nirvana.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Coldplay", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Oasis", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Radiohead", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Beatles", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Smiths", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "dance-pop": {"genre": "dance-pop", "country_code": "mx", "country_name": "Mexico", "summary": "Dance-pop is a style of electronic dance music and a subgenre of pop music that evolved from Disco, circa 1981, that combines dance beats with a pop/R'n'B song structure. Because there is such an emphasis on fully-formed songs in dance-pop, it's often viewed as a separate classification unto itself apart from pure dance. Dance-pop is also closely related to the teen pop and Eurodance movements in the mid-1980s and late 1990s, the rise of boy bands and girl groups, and the reintroduction of the vocoder and similar such innovations.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "AD\u00c9LA", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Ariana Grande", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Britney Spears", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Chappell Roan", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Charli xcx", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Dua Lipa", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Jimin", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Justin Bieber", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "KATSEYE", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Katy Perry", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Lady Gaga", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Madonna", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "electronic": {"genre": "electronic", "country_code": "mx", "country_name": "Mexico", "summary": "Electronic music refers to music that emphasizes the use of electronic musical instruments or electronic music technology as a central aspect of the sound of the music. Historically, electronic music was considered to be any music created with the use of electronic musical instruments or electronic processing, but in modern times, that distinction has been lost because almost all recorded music today, and the majority of live music performances, depend on extensive use of electronics.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "BTS", "streams": 363333, "best_position": 44}, {"artist": "Belanova", "streams": 274334, "best_position": 84}, {"artist": "Rauw Alejandro", "streams": 261365, "best_position": 97}, {"artist": "Arctic Monkeys", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Billie Eilish", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Britney Spears", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Charli xcx", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Daddy Yankee", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Daft Punk", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Dua Lipa", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Gorillaz", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Jimin", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "electropop": {"genre": "electropop", "country_code": "mx", "country_name": "Mexico", "summary": "Electropop is a type of electronic pop music which features crackly synthesizers prominently in the mix.   Electropop has become an increasingly common term for this music post-2000 whereas in earlier years, synthpop was probably the more common term for pop music using synthesizers.\n\nWhen Kraftwerk first appeared in the mid-1970's, their music was described as electronic body music (ebm) in Germany, Krautrock in England, and technopop in Japan.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Belanova", "streams": 274334, "best_position": 84}, {"artist": "AD\u00c9LA", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Billie Eilish", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Britney Spears", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Chappell Roan", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Charli xcx", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Dua Lipa", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Gorillaz", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "KATSEYE", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Katy Perry", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Lady Gaga", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Madonna", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "hip-hop": {"genre": "hip-hop", "country_code": "mx", "country_name": "Mexico", "summary": "Hip-Hop, also spelled Hip Hop or HipHop is a rhythm focused popular music style, originating from New York in The 70s. The term rap is sometimes used synonymously with Hip-Hop music. Hip-hop arose when DJs began isolating the percussion break from funk or disco songs for audiences to dance to.\nIt is now seen as a worldwide and popular genre ranging from American Mainstream (e.g. Eminem, Lil Wayne) to British Underground (e.g. Wiley, EMC Junkie ect).", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Neton Vega", "streams": 3095193, "best_position": 2}, {"artist": "Junior H", "streams": 2924292, "best_position": 8}, {"artist": "Bad Bunny", "streams": 1288158, "best_position": 48}, {"artist": "Natanael Cano", "streams": 1142890, "best_position": 16}, {"artist": "J Balvin", "streams": 315076, "best_position": 65}, {"artist": "Rauw Alejandro", "streams": 261365, "best_position": 97}, {"artist": "Agust D", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Alvaro Diaz", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "BLACKPINK", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Daddy Yankee", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Daft Punk", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Doja Cat", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "k-pop": {"genre": "k-pop", "country_code": "mx", "country_name": "Mexico", "summary": "K-pop means Korean pop, which is\u00a0a musical genre, sometimes described more as an umbrella term, consisting of different music styles, including hip-hop, rap, jazz, r&b, dance, rock music and ballads. The name for the genre is first recorded in English around 1990\u201395. Strongly influenced by Western popular music, K-pop took off in 1992 with Seo Taiji and Boys, who incorporated rap, rock, and dance elements into Korean popular music.\nModern\u00a0K-pop \"idol\" culture\u00a0began later in the 1990s, as K-pop idol music grew into a\u00a0subculture.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "BTS", "streams": 363333, "best_position": 44}, {"artist": "Agust D", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "BLACKPINK", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "CORTIS", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "ENHYPEN", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "ILLIT", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Jimin", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Jin", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Jung Kook", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "KATSEYE", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "LE SSERAFIM", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "NewJeans", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "latin": {"genre": "latin", "country_code": "mx", "country_name": "Mexico", "summary": "Latin American music or Latin music encompasses rhythms and styles originated or related to Latin America and its influence in the United States and several European countries such as Spain or Portugal. Some critics have defined Latin music as an incorporation of four elements: music style, geography, cultural background of the artist and language. The first of those encapsulates all music styles generated from Latin countries, such as salsa, merengue.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "KAROL G", "streams": 2725839, "best_position": 1}, {"artist": "Tito Double P", "streams": 1382349, "best_position": 21}, {"artist": "Bad Bunny", "streams": 1288158, "best_position": 48}, {"artist": "Natanael Cano", "streams": 1142890, "best_position": 16}, {"artist": "J Balvin", "streams": 315076, "best_position": 65}, {"artist": "Belanova", "streams": 274334, "best_position": 84}, {"artist": "Maluma", "streams": 265632, "best_position": 92}, {"artist": "Caifanes", "streams": 262074, "best_position": 96}, {"artist": "Rauw Alejandro", "streams": 261365, "best_position": 97}, {"artist": "Alvaro Diaz", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Caf\u00e9 Tacvba", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Daddy Yankee", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "new wave": {"genre": "new wave", "country_code": "mx", "country_name": "Mexico", "summary": "New wave is today a quite broad umbrella term describing popular music from around 1977 to 1986. But originally it was a slim sub genre of Western popular music that arose in the United Kingdom about 1977-78. It had close ties to punk rock and fairly strong influences of the musical style that had been invented and continuously developed throughout the 1970s: reggae.\n\nThe term new wave was first a kind of description of a more musical and lyric wise complex music than punk.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Harry Styles", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Madonna", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Paramore", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Soda Stereo", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Cure", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Smiths", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Strokes", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "pop": {"genre": "pop", "country_code": "mx", "country_name": "Mexico", "summary": "Pop music is a broad-term for many different types of music: The term is flexible, and the music labeled \"pop\" changes frequently. It usually refers to popular, appealing and mostly mainstream music with emphasis on catchy melodies and an accessible style, with songs that tend to have a short to medium length. Some subgenres may include synthpop, electropop, bubblegum, sophisti-pop, hyperpop and many others.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Junior H", "streams": 2924292, "best_position": 8}, {"artist": "KAROL G", "streams": 2725839, "best_position": 1}, {"artist": "BTS", "streams": 363333, "best_position": 44}, {"artist": "J Balvin", "streams": 315076, "best_position": 65}, {"artist": "Belanova", "streams": 274334, "best_position": 84}, {"artist": "Maluma", "streams": 265632, "best_position": 92}, {"artist": "AD\u00c9LA", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Alvaro Diaz", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Arctic Monkeys", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Ariana Grande", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "BLACKPINK", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Billie Eilish", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "post-punk": {"genre": "post-punk", "country_code": "mx", "country_name": "Mexico", "summary": "Post-punk (originally called new musick) is a broad genre of music that emerged in late 1977 in the wake of punk rock. Post-punk musicians departed from punk's fundamental elements and raw simplicity, instead adopting a broader, more experimental approach that encompassed a variety of avant-garde sensibilities and non-rock influences. Inspired by punk's energy and do it yourself ethic but determined to break from rock cliches, artists experimented with styles like funk.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Caifanes", "streams": 262074, "best_position": 96}, {"artist": "Arctic Monkeys", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Mac DeMarco", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "My Chemical Romance", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Soda Stereo", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Cure", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Smiths", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Strokes", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "r&b": {"genre": "r&b", "country_code": "mx", "country_name": "Mexico", "summary": "R&B is a musical genre that began to develop as a distinct style in the early 1950s. Originally known as rhythm and blues, it was primarily created by African American musicians and drew influence from both blues and early rock 'n' roll, with significant interaction between these genres. Over time, musicians from different backgrounds adopted the style and introduced new elements. In the 1950s, artists like Muddy Waters contributed to shaping the genre by emphasizing faster melodies and energetic rhythms.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "KAROL G", "streams": 2725839, "best_position": 1}, {"artist": "Ariana Grande", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Billie Eilish", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Britney Spears", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Bruno Mars", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Daft Punk", "streams": null, "best_